WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:06.100
From huge reveals about Vecna and The Mind
Flayer to a bombshell ending for Eleven and

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.250
the gang, the final volume of Stranger Things
Season 4 has finally arrived!

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:15.959
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining the big season finale,

00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:20.460
revealing some hidden secrets you might have
missed, and what to expect in Season 5.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.430
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:28.030
At the end of Season 4, during his villain's
monologue, Vecna reveals he's been the evil

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.759
mastermind behind everything all along.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:35.790
After Eleven sent One into the Upside Down,
he explored the new world and eventually came

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.850
across a mass of unformed particles.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:44.440
Using his powers, he shaped these into a giant
spider form, The Mind Flayer, basing the monster's

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.020
look on the Black Widow spiders he so admired
as a child.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.890
I saw a means to realize my potential.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.850
To transcend my human form.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:59.050
In fact, the young Henry Creel already had
a vision for the monster he would go on to

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.980
create many years later, and his drawing is
uncannily similar to the one that Will made

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.430
in Season 2.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:10.070
This makes sense because we know now that
the Mind Flayer was invented by One, and he

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.610
was therefore controlling Will at that moment.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.510
Back in the Upside Down, Vecna then had to
wait for Eleven to eventually open up a gate

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:23.160
again to the real world, which she did accidentally
when she first made contact with a Demogorgon

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.710
in Season 1.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:30.370
But because El fought back each time and closed
Vecna's access to the world in the first two

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.710
seasons, he decided on a plan to take Eleven's
portal-opening powers for himself in Season

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.710
3.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.310
I sought a means to open my own doors.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.440
I sought your power.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.960
He achieved this through the Spider Monster,
which attacked Eleven and took her powers,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.620
which were in turn transferred to Vecna who
used them to begin opening gates between the

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.090
Upside Down and Hawkins in Season 4 whenever
he made a kill.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:00.270
Vecna's plan was to open four gates by killing
four teens, something hinted at through his

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:05.890
clock which always chimed four times whenever
it appeared to one of his intended victims.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.439
The significance of the number four might
also be a reference to the Four Horsemen of

00:02:10.439 --> 00:02:15.680
the Apocalypse, which certainly seems appropriate
given the way the final season ends after

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.969
the four gates have been opened.

00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:22.950
And notice how in Volume 1, the clocks at
both Hawkins Lab and the Creel House were

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:28.540
at 3 o'clock at critical moments, a clue to
the three victims that Vecna had claimed by

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.340
the end of the first part of the season.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.140
The Hawkins crew themselves come up with a
four-phase plan they hope will defeat Vecna,

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:41.040
the problem being that as good as it might
have been, he already knew what they had planned.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.569
By appearing to Max as a vision of an angry
Lucas, Vecna traps her in a twisted version

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:51.659
of what should be a happy memory for her of
the Snow Ball dance at the end of Season 2.

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:56.249
There was some ominous foreshadowing of this
moment in the way Season 2 ended with the

00:02:56.249 --> 00:03:01.819
camera flipping over to a shot of the Shadow
Monster watching over the Ball in the Upside

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:02.819
Down.

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:07.299
Vecna then throws Max across the room and
pins her against a wall, just like Eleven

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:11.750
did to him in the Hawkins Lab and to the Demogorgon
in the school.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:17.370
However, when Eleven manages break into Max's
nightmare, she propels Vecna into the air,

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:22.450
twisting him around, and curling her fingers
and wrist, similar to what he did to her years

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.120
earlier in Hawkins Lab.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:29.930
Vecna quickly recovers from this and overpowers
Eleven, sending her into his mindscape, and

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.870
trapping her with his vines.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:36.629
This is exactly what Brenner warned Eleven
about when he said she wasn't strong enough

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:41.769
to confront Vecna so quickly after regaining
her powers and that she needed to learn more.

00:03:41.769 --> 00:03:43.419
If you want to stop One.

00:03:43.419 --> 00:03:44.989
You will need to do more than run.

00:03:44.989 --> 00:03:46.560
You will need to fly.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:51.659
At that moment, Eleven wanted to leave immediately
to help her friends who she knew were in danger

00:03:51.659 --> 00:03:56.719
in Hawkins, something very reminiscent of
how Luke Skywalker wanted to leave his training

00:03:56.719 --> 00:04:01.419
with Yoda early to go and help Leia and Han
Solo in The Empire Strikes Back.

00:04:01.419 --> 00:04:06.569
And there's also shades of Palpatine in Vecna
when he tells Eleven he wants her to watch

00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:12.510
him execute his evil plan, similar to how
the Emperor tells Luke to watch while he destroys

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.519
the Rebellion.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.862
I want you to watch.

00:04:14.862 --> 00:04:19.009
You will witness the end of your insignificant
rebellion.

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:24.660
At this point, Vecna has broken Eleven's will,
and it's not until Mike tells her how much

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:29.240
he loves her, that Vecna's vines shrink away
and she frees herself.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.879
Similar to how Max needed happy memories to
escape Vecna's grip previously, Mike's heartfelt

00:04:34.879 --> 00:04:37.250
words are what El needs to break free.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.819
The moment calls back to Will's painting where
he explained to Mike that because he's the

00:04:41.819 --> 00:04:46.390
one who leads the group, he has a coat of
arms with a heart on it, as he's the one who

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.009
holds everyone together.

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:49.970
Without heart, we'd all fall apart.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.970
Even El.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.600
By the way, in Season 1 after Will went missing,
Mike was browsing some similar paintings by

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.550
Will of the D&amp;D crew going up against a dragon.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.939
Another interesting detail about Will's painting
is that when he shows it to Mike he claims

00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:05.090
that Eleven asked him to draw it.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.259
Did you paint this?

00:05:07.259 --> 00:05:08.280
El l asked me to.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.319
She commissioned it, basically.

00:05:09.319 --> 00:05:11.259
I mean, she told me what to draw.

00:05:11.259 --> 00:05:14.900
But this doesn't match El's voiceover in the
first episode:

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.750
Will is painting a lot, but he won't show
me what he's working on.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.570
It's possible Will is embarrassed to tell
Mike why he really drew the painting, so he's

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.720
pretending El asked him to do it instead.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:31.150
The combined might of Eleven pinning Vecna
in his mindscape, Murray flaming the demogorgons

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:36.169
in Russia, and Steve and Robin's use of Molotov
cocktails, weakens the villain to the point

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:39.860
that Nancy can finish him off with some close-range
gun shots.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.610
This sends him flying through the Creel House
attic window to the ground below where he

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.039
appears to be defeated.

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:49.629
However, when they go downstairs, his body
has disappeared.

00:05:49.629 --> 00:05:54.729
The moment is a homage to Michael Myers and
the first Halloween movie where after being

00:05:54.729 --> 00:05:59.360
shot and falling off a balcony, he appeared
to be dead on the ground below.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:03.610
However, moments later his body disappeared,
proving the villain was still alive.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:09.030
There were also a few other Halloween references
in Volume 2, such as the way Vecna moves his

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:14.680
head just before his confrontation with Eleven,
in a nod to Michael Myer's iconic head tilt.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.169
And Eddie, of course, donned a Michael Myers
mask briefly as well.

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:23.590
When El finally gets back to Hawkins, she
goes to visit Max who's now in a coma.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:29.330
The book Lucas reads to Max from is "The Talisman"
by Stephen King and Peter Straub, a story

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:34.580
in which the protagonist whose mother is dying
travels into a parallel universe where Twinners

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.660
or doppelgangers of an individual also exist.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.849
Interestingly, The Talisman is also the Duffer
Brothers' and Steven Spielberg's next project

00:06:42.849 --> 00:06:44.180
with Netflix.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:49.539
Although El tries to go into the Void to connect
with Max, she gets no response, and I think

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:56.020
Max's recovery could be contingent on Eleven's
eventual victory over Vecna in Season 5.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.920
Notice how Max tells Lucas she can't see or
feel anything after Vecna's attack.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.080
When One kills, he consumes.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.099
He takes everything from his victims.

00:07:05.099 --> 00:07:06.500
Their memories, their abilities.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:11.520
So, it may be that his defeat will somehow
release Max's consciousness back to her as

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:16.630
there have been numerous allusions and references
to how Vecna absorbs his victims.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:19.680
With each life I took, I grew stronger.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.720
They were becoming a part of me.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.439
And the Coke bottle Eleven finds under her
bed at Hopper's old cabin is a call-back to

00:07:26.439 --> 00:07:32.020
the time she spun the bottle with Max in Season
3 and used her abilities to remotely spy on

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.960
what Mike and the other boys were doing and
saying.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:39.919
The memory is especially sad for El because
she knows that right now she can't reach Max

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:41.240
even with her powers.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:46.710
Of course, we have to talk about Eddie who
made the ultimate sacrifice in Season 4.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:51.259
There were various clues earlier on to his
fate, such as him talking in the first episode

00:07:51.259 --> 00:07:55.719
about how he'd finally graduate and hand over
the reins of The Hellfire Club…

00:07:55.719 --> 00:07:57.419
This year is my year.

00:07:57.419 --> 00:08:02.650
You boys are the future of Hellfire.
…and how he kept pointing out he wasn't

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:07.290
a hero:
I see danger and I just turn heel and run.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.639
There is no shame in running, don't try to
be heroes.

00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:15.830
The even sadder thing is that Eddie is still
being demonised and blamed for several murders

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.249
in Hawkins by the media and the community.

00:08:18.249 --> 00:08:22.819
Fortunately, Dustin, who knows the truth,
was at least was able to tell Eddie's uncle

00:08:22.819 --> 00:08:25.289
that he died a hero saving the town.

00:08:25.289 --> 00:08:30.699
As for Eleven, she got an emotional reunion
with her Dad in his cabin, and notice how

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:35.590
she was still keeping her door open a few
inches, just like she did in the opening episode

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:36.740
of Season 4.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.200
I kept the door open three inches.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.850
And in the very final scene, Will reveals
he knows Vecna is still alive through the

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:46.410
connection he still has with the Mind Flayer.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:50.340
I can still remember what he thinks, and how
he thinks.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.860
And he's not going to stop.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.230
Not until he's taken everything.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:55.230
And everyone.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:09:00.850
And the hairs on his neck stand up just before
that final shot, revealing that the Upside

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.790
Down has truly broken through to the real
world.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.530
The flowers in this field are rotting away,
similar to how a pumpkin field began to decay

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:12.010
after the Upside Down's tunnels reached them
in Season 2.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:17.220
You can also see the Upside Down's characteristic
red lightning flashing over here, where the

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.430
main breach appears to have occurred.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:24.110
This basically confirms the vision Vecna gave
to Nancy about what was to come:

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:25.660
Downtown on fire.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.700
Dead soldiers.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.710
This giant creature with a gaping mouth.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.710
There were so many monsters.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.910
An army.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:38.380
It sounds like in Season 5, we could get a
huge new monster and a slew of other Upside

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.790
Down creatures.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.400
Nancy's comments about her family, including
Mike, also sound very ominous.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.910
He showed me my mom.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:46.910
Holly.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:47.910
Mike.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:49.060
They were all…

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:54.570
And as powerful as Eleven is, I don't think
she can take on a whole army from the Upside

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:59.380
Down, which means I think she'll need to do
something on a different level to defeat Vecna.

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:04.620
One possible hint is this curious moment where
Nancy points out Argyle picking some mushrooms

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.010
in the woods just outside the cabin.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:12.060
Some mushroom varieties can have hallucinogenic
effects and there could be a possible connection

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:17.700
here to lucid dreaming, potentially a different
way for Eleven to battle with Vecna on a psychic

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.700
level.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.630
Another possibility, given all of the Back
To The Future references in the series, is

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:27.540
that Eleven will perform some kind of time
travel, perhaps to stop Henry turning into

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.970
a villain in the first place.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:34.030
And there's a big clue to why I think that's
happening in Season 5 in Nancy's vision that

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.450
Vecna gave her of the future.

